What is Hermetia Illucens?
Hermetia Illucens, commonly known as the Black Soldier Fly, is an insect species primarily found in tropical and subtropical regions. Its larvae are highly efficient in decomposing organic waste such as food scraps and animal manure, offering significant environmental and economic benefits. Rich in protein and fat, these larvae serve as a sustainable source of animal feed, while adult flies are ecologically safe as they do not feed or transmit diseases.
